cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use xingo-statla, please cite it using these metadata. Each release is archived on Zenodo with its own DOI."
# TODO(owner): add `doi:` and `identifiers:` (concept DOI and version DOI) once Zenodo has archived the first release, as in xingo-extprec.
type: software
title: "xingo-statla: updatable and matrix-free linear algebra for statistics"
abstract: "Updatable and matrix-free linear algebra for statistics in pure Rust: a thin QR with explicit Q and a Cholesky factor updated in place when rows, columns or rank-1 terms arrive or leave, with transactional failures; the randomized SVD of Halko, Martinsson and Tropp with a reproducible generator; a truncated SVD by thick-restart Golub-Kahan-Lanczos bidiagonalization; and ARPACK-style eigsh/eigs by Krylov-Schur restarted Lanczos/Arnoldi, with shift-invert over sparse factorizations and an inertia count. Generic in the scalar type, over a linear-operator trait. Part of the Xingó project."
authors:
  - family-names: Leite
    given-names: André
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/StrategicProjects/xingo-statla"
url: "https://strategicprojects.github.io/xingo-statla/"
version: 0.1.0
# TODO(owner): `date-released:` with the date of publication.
keywords:
  - updating matrix factorizations
  - QR update
  - Cholesky downdate
  - randomized SVD
  - truncated SVD
  - Lanczos bidiagonalization
  - Krylov-Schur
  - sparse eigenvalues
  - statistics
  - Rust
